1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,415
Two days in, 1,000+ GitHub stars:

2
00:00:02,435 --> 00:00:03,756
Meta has open-sourced the firmware

3
00:00:03,776 --> 00:00:06,330
and SDK for building Muse peripherals.

4
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:07,756
On October 2, US time,

5
00:00:07,776 --> 00:00:10,177
Nat Friedman and Alexandr Wang of Meta

6
00:00:10,197 --> 00:00:12,492
Superintelligence Labs announced Muse Gadgets on X:

7
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:14,913
let anyone build hardware

8
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:16,860
for Meta's personal AI agent, Muse.

9
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:19,151
Two things are open: ESP32 firmware

10
00:00:19,171 --> 00:00:20,713
and a Linux SDK. Dev boards

11
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:22,622
and Raspberry Pis both work;

12
00:00:22,642 --> 00:00:24,790
the code is Apache 2.0.

13
00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:26,907
The flow: get an SDK token,

14
00:00:26,927 --> 00:00:29,143
flash the firmware, pair in the Muse app.

15
00:00:29,163 --> 00:00:31,996
Nat Friedman's tip: hand the repo to a coding agent

16
00:00:32,016 --> 00:00:34,530
and let it build the peripheral.

17
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,934
The site lists eight example projects:

18
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:39,383
a Raspberry Pi for Home Assistant, a round touchscreen

19
00:00:39,403 --> 00:00:42,061
with push-to-talk, an HDMI TV stick coming soon,

20
00:00:42,081 --> 00:00:44,530
and a color e-ink briefing display.

21
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:46,202
Meta built one too: Muse Home Link.

22
00:00:46,222 --> 00:00:48,340
It plugs in over USB-C,

23
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:49,978
runs an ESP32-C5, joins home Wi-Fi,

24
00:00:49,998 --> 00:00:52,247
and community skills

25
00:00:52,267 --> 00:00:54,760
can let Muse turn on lights or control a TV.

26
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:57,428
Meta made a batch of 5,000,

27
00:00:57,448 --> 00:00:58,716
free for subscribers.

28
00:00:58,736 --> 00:01:00,486
But the site says: US only, one per person,

29
00:01:00,506 --> 00:01:03,450
first come first served, shipping in October.

30
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:05,351
But Apache 2.0 covers only the code.

31
00:01:05,371 --> 00:01:06,644
The token terms say: personal,

32
00:01:06,664 --> 00:01:08,895
non-commercial use, at most 50 devices, no selling,

33
00:01:08,915 --> 00:01:11,500
and Meta can revoke access at any time.

34
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:12,584
The hands are open source.

35
00:01:12,604 --> 00:01:14,770
The brain stays in Meta's cloud.
